//
// The profile's derived bounds agree with the builders at every ladder point.
// Host-only: constructs IR, never compiles, never touches a device.
//
// `[2026-08-20]` The first `full` profile (devq 427) found three bounds the
// case matrix's 64..16384 ladder crosses: the FlashAttention parallel_seq
// floor (coarse and fused below 256), the attention GEMMs' fixed-tile
// multiple (offload and runlist below 512), and the softmax's L1 row width
// (runlist at 16384). study/profiles.skip_reason now carries each as a
// derived structural skip -- the same standing as fused's packing bound, the
// builder raising before aircc is reached -- with every constant re-derived
// from the refusing builder's SOURCE by ast in run_study_host_tests. This
// suite is the other altitude: WITH air, for all four modes at all nine
// lengths, skip_reason says "skip" exactly when the mode's config or module
// construction refuses, and "run" exactly when every module builds. Both
// directions are non-vacuous per bounded mode, and the refusal messages are
// the mechanisms the bounds cite.
//
// RUN: python3 %S/builders/test_profile_bounds.py | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: profile bound tests: 3/3 passed
